.TH "GF-ADMIN-USERS-ADMIN-UPDATE-USER-PERMISSIONS" "1" "May 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-admin-users-admin-update-user-permissions - Sets permissions for user


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf admin-users admin-update-user-permissions [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets permissions for user

.PP
Only works with Basic Authentication (username and password). See introduction for an explanation. If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled, you need to have a permission with action \fBusers.permissions:update\fR and scope \fBglobal.users:*\fR\&.

.PP
Body schema (AdminUpdateUserPermissionsForm):
  isGrafanaAdmin  boolean

.PP
Response schema (AdminUpdateUserPermissionsOK.Payload):
  message  string


